{
 "note": "Extra circuits for the lap simulator: which candidate track becomes which simulator track, and the real laps used for the quality check. Read by scripts/sim/build-geometry-extra.mjs. Candidates: scripts/sim/data/tracks/.",
 "declared": "Check per track: simulate the production WEC class cars (LMH, LMDh, LMGT3; nearest fitted season, 2025 or 2026) on the track with the mean track factor of that class's fitted tracks and the weather of the real lap. Compare with the fastest clean dry qualifying lap per series, season (2023 to 2026) and car class. Borrowed cars: IMSA GTP uses the LMDh car; IMSA GTD, ELMS LMGT3, IGTC Pro, GTWC Pro, ADAC GT Masters and Nürburgring SP 9 use the LMGT3 car. Pass: at least one row and RMS error at or below 3.0 % (the error of this geometry method on known tracks: 3.0 to 3.2 % RMS in scripts/sim/data/tracks/method-check.json on the source branch). Otherwise the track is marked ⚠️ and fit = false. Baseline: none needed, no model is changed. Not checked: sectors, corner minimum speeds, speed traps.",
 "declared2": "F1 car positions of a 2018 to 2021 qualifying session were built into tracks with the production builder and its production smoothing (scripts/sim/build-geometry-f1-history.mjs). Method check on four production circuits built the same way from 2025 sessions (Spielberg, Silverstone, Monza, Hungaroring): lap time within 0.3 to 0.9 % of the production track with the F1 car (RMS 0.6 %) and within 0.3 % with the LMGT3 car. Car-free geometry flag: the lateral acceleration that the pole lap's real speed implies on the built curvature. The four production circuits give 5.0 to 6.6 g; the limit is 7.0 g. This limit was set after the values of the new tracks were seen, so it is a description, not a blind test. A track from F1 positions replaces the map line only when it is inside the limit: Nürburgring Grand Prix (6.8 g) and Sakhir Outer (6.8 g). Outside the limit, the map line is kept: Hockenheim (8.7 g), Mugello (8.7 g), Portimão (7.6 g). Paul Ricard F1 layout (7.6 g) has no map line and is stored with ⚠️. Extra check row for F1-position tracks: the F1 pole of that session against the F1 car of the nearest fitted season (2023), mean F1 track factor, no per-track drag factor. Borrowed-season car: real 2023 poles were 1.8 to 4.3 % slower than 2020 poles on circuits raced dry in both years, so this row mostly measures the car. Also added as a borrowed LMGT3 row: GT World Challenge Europe Endurance, Pro class. The pass rule is unchanged.",
 "declared3": "Timing71 sweep over every series (owner request): a row counts when its car model names a GT3 car (not GT4, GT2 or Cup) or its class is IMSA GTD or IGTC Pro/Overall; the series label in the table can be wrong (GT World Challenge Sprint rows sit under other series names), so the car model decides. Fastest such row per track and season, added only where the track had no LMGT3 row for that season. Seasons 2018 to 2022 are used only for a track with no 2023 to 2026 row and are labelled \"older\". DPi and GTLM rows are not used (no matching fitted car). A row is dropped when the official lap length divided by its lap time is outside 120 to 215 km/h (another layout of the same venue, for example Le Mans Bugatti). Rows stored under the venue id \"nordschleife\" with laps of 99 to 125 s are not used: the venue label cannot be trusted there. The pass rule is unchanged.",
 "passRmsPct": 3,
 "lapSource": "Timing71 rows; derived table scripts/sim/data/laps/t71-bests-counts.json on branch lapsim-laps/all-laps-2026-11-11 at commit 47c8822 (raw files are not in git)",
 "limits": [
  "Start line, direction, sectors and corner numbers are not verified (start = first mapped point).",
  "Height comes from a 30 m ground grid, smoothed over 150 m: crests and dips shorter than that are missing. No banking (Daytona).",
  "The driven line is a model line, not compared with a real driven line.",
  "Lap-time error only. Corner minimum speed, end-of-straight speed and sectors are not checked (rule 3.4): a pass does not prove the parts of the lap.",
  "Surface changes in scripts/sim/data/tracks/track-state.json were not applied to the reference rows: Laguna Seca 2023 rows are on the old surface.",
  "Error includes geometry, car and borrowed-car error together; rows with a borrowed car say less about the track.",
  "The Timing71 venue id \"nurburgring-gp\" holds three layouts; rows were split by lap time (80–90 s sprint, 105–125 s Grand Prix, 470–520 s 24 Hours lap). No Grand Prix lap of a GT3 or Hypercar class exists in the table."
 ],
